# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo when it archives a
# release. Keep `version` in step with `metalog_geocoding.__version__`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use metalog-geocoding, please cite it using the metadata below, and
  also cite the data sources listed under "references".
type: software
title: "metalog-geocoding: an offline reverse geocoder for land, sea and distance to coast"
authors:
  - family-names: Kuhn
    given-names: Michael
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2841-872X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/grp-bork/metalog-geocoding"
url: "https://github.com/grp-bork/metalog-geocoding"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  An offline reverse geocoder. Given a latitude and longitude it returns either
  a land location (continent, country, first-level administrative region;
  Natural Earth) or an ocean/sea (IHO Sea Areas plus the Longhurst
  biogeochemical province; MarineRegions), falls back to the nearest polygon
  for near-shore points, and measures the signed distance to the coast (GSHHG).
  Developed for the Metalog metagenomics database to annotate sample
  coordinates.
keywords:
  - reverse geocoding
  - geocoding
  - marine regions
  - Longhurst provinces
  - metagenomics
  - sample metadata
references:
  - type: data
    title: Natural Earth
    authors:
      - name: Natural Earth
    url: "https://www.naturalearthdata.com/"
    license: CC0-1.0
  - type: data
    title: IHO Sea Areas, version 3
    authors:
      - name: Flanders Marine Institute
    url: "https://www.marineregions.org/"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
  - type: data
    title: Longhurst Provinces, version 4
    authors:
      - name: Flanders Marine Institute
    url: "https://www.marineregions.org/"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
  - type: book
    title: Ecological Geography of the Sea
    authors:
      - family-names: Longhurst
        given-names: Alan R.
  - type: article
    title: A global, self-consistent, hierarchical, high-resolution shoreline database
    authors:
      - family-names: Wessel
        given-names: Paul
      - family-names: Smith
        given-names: Walter H. F.
    journal: Journal of Geophysical Research
    volume: 101
    issue: B4
    start: 8741
    end: 8743
    year: 1996
    doi: 10.1029/96JB00104
  - type: data
    title: GeoNames
    authors:
      - name: GeoNames
    url: "https://www.geonames.org/"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
